From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Chulo <cchulo.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus-ally: hold the ROG Xbox Ally X20 top-right key
 (KEY_PROG2) for 250 ms

The X20's MCU reports the top-right (capture) button as "5a a0" followed
by "5a 00" about 1 ms later, however long the button is physically held
(measured on an RC74XA with vm/guest/watch-buttons.py: press at
2.002 s, release at 2.003 s). Patch 0012 passed that straight through as
a 1 ms KEY_PROG2 tap.

InputPlumber (0.78.0, the SteamOS daemon) maps that key to its
"Screenshot" capability, and its Steam Deck target has no screenshot
button, so it synthesises a chord: Guide pressed at once, R1 pressed
160 ms later; on release, R1 released after 160 ms and Guide after
240 ms (src/input/target/steam_deck.rs). With a 1 ms tap the R1 release
is queued 8 ms after the press, i.e. for t = 168 ms, before the R1
press has fired at t = 160 ms. When that press fires, write_event()
"clears any stale queued events for this capability" and deletes the
pending R1 release. R1 stays held in the virtual Deck pad until the
real bumper is pressed, so the next Xbox (Guide) press is Steam+R1 and
takes a screenshot too. Reproduced on the X20: Xbox works from boot,
breaks after one capture press, recovers after one R1 press. A held key
never hits this because its release is queued after the chord started.

Report KEY_PROG2 pressed when 0xa0 arrives, ignore the MCU's immediate
release, and release the key from a delayed work item 250 ms later. The
chord then runs Guide 0 ms, R1 160 ms, R1 up 410 ms, Guide up 490 ms,
with nothing overlapping. A second press within the 250 ms extends the
hold instead of producing a second tap, which is fine for a screenshot
key. The work is cancelled in ally_x_remove(), before the devm-managed
input device goes away (patch 0013 ordering).

Only the Ally X input path changes; the "ASUS ROG Ally Config" path
for older Allys still reports 0xa0 as a plain key with the MCU's own
release.

Derived from:
- ShadowBlip/InputPlumber v0.78.0 src/input/target/steam_deck.rs
  (GamepadButton::Screenshot chord: Guide at 0 ms, RightBumper at
  160 ms, release RightBumper at 160 ms and Guide at 240 ms;
  write_event(): MIN_FRAME_TIME 8 ms requeue of same-frame releases and
  the "Clear any stale up events for this capability" retain that drops
  the pending RightBumper release) and src/input/target/mod.rs (the
  4 ms poll loop that replays scheduled events through write_event),
  https://github.com/ShadowBlip/InputPlumber
- vm/guest/watch-buttons.py capture on the owner's RC74XA, 2026-10-31
  (x20-data/buttons-xbox.log: "5a a0" / KEY_PROG2 press at 2.002 s,
  "5a 00" / release at 2.003 s)
- Linux workqueue API (include/linux/workqueue.h: INIT_DELAYED_WORK,
  mod_delayed_work, cancel_delayed_work_sync) in the same tree

Base: linux-integration 7.2.7-valve2 plus 0010..0014.
---
 drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
index 25cc5eb..94ed877 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@
  * to userspace.
  */
 #define ALLY_X20_KEY_RIGHT 0xa0
+/*
+ * The MCU reports 0xa0 and its 0x00 release about 1 ms apart, however long
+ * the button is held. The key is reported pressed for at least this long so
+ * userspace sees a press a human could have made. InputPlumber's Steam Deck
+ * target turns a "Screenshot" press into a Guide+R1 chord spread over 160 ms
+ * and loses the R1 release when the key goes up before the chord has
+ * started, leaving R1 held until the real bumper is pressed.
+ */
+#define ALLY_X20_KEY_HOLD_MS 250
 
 #define FEATURE_KBD_LED_REPORT_ID1 0x5d
 #define FEATURE_KBD_LED_REPORT_ID2 0x5e
@@ -497,6 +506,8 @@ struct ally_x_device {
 	/* Set if the QAM and AC buttons emit Xbox and Xbox+A */
 	bool qam_btns_steam_mode;
 	bool update_ff;
+	/* Deferred release of KEY_PROG2 (X20 top-right key), see ALLY_X20_KEY_HOLD_MS */
+	struct delayed_work x20_key_release;
 };
 
 struct ally_rgb_dev {
@@ -1620,8 +1631,16 @@ static int ally_x_raw_event(struct ally_x_device *ally_x, struct hid_report *rep
 			input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_F16, data[1] == 0xA6);
 			input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_PROG1, data[1] == 0x38 || data[1] == 0x93);
 		}
-		/* X20 top-right key: one plain key in both qam modes, no chord */
-		input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_PROG2, data[1] == ALLY_X20_KEY_RIGHT);
+		/*
+		 * X20 top-right key: one plain key in both qam modes, no chord.
+		 * The MCU's own release follows the press within 1 ms and is
+		 * ignored; ally_x_x20_key_release() releases the key instead.
+		 */
+		if (data[1] == ALLY_X20_KEY_RIGHT) {
+			input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_PROG2, 1);
+			mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &ally_x->x20_key_release,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(ALLY_X20_KEY_HOLD_MS));
+		}
 		/* QAM long press */
 		input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_F17, data[1] == 0xA7);
 		/* QAM long press released */
@@ -1633,6 +1652,15 @@ static int ally_x_raw_event(struct ally_x_device *ally_x, struct hid_report *rep
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void ally_x_x20_key_release(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct ally_x_device *ally_x =
+		container_of(to_delayed_work(work), struct ally_x_device, x20_key_release);
+
+	input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_PROG2, 0);
+	input_sync(ally_x->input);
+}
+
 static struct input_dev *ally_x_alloc_input_dev(struct hid_device *hdev,
 						const char *name_suffix)
 {
@@ -1807,6 +1835,7 @@ static struct ally_x_device *ally_x_create(struct hid_device *hdev)
 
 	ally_x->hdev = hdev;
 	INIT_WORK(&ally_x->output_worker, ally_x_work);
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&ally_x->x20_key_release, ally_x_x20_key_release);
 	spin_lock_init(&ally_x->lock);
 	ally_x->output_worker_initialized = true;
 	ally_x->qam_btns_steam_mode =
@@ -1864,6 +1893,7 @@ static void ally_x_remove(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	ally_x->output_worker_initialized = false;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ally_x->lock, flags);
 	cancel_work_sync(&ally_x->output_worker);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&ally_x->x20_key_release);
 	sysfs_remove_file(&hdev->dev.kobj, &dev_attr_ally_x_qam_mode.attr);
 }
 
